1
00:00:02,127 --> 00:00:05,088
Well, <i>Lords of the Ring</i> trilogy, if you see it back to back,

2
00:00:05,172 --> 00:00:06,608
Yeah... it's really long, but it's good.

3
00:00:06,632 --> 00:00:07,758
Dunder Mifflin, this is Pam.

4
00:00:07,841 --> 00:00:09,218
<i>Pam, it's Michael. Help me.</i>

5
00:00:09,301 --> 00:00:11,386
<i>I need help right now!</i> Michael, what's wrong?

6
00:00:11,470 --> 00:00:13,347
<i>I'm hurt. I have hurt myself.</i>

7
00:00:13,764 --> 00:00:15,599
<i>Oh, my God!</i> Okay, wait, wait, wait, wait!

8
00:00:15,682 --> 00:00:17,434
<i>Oh, this is not looking good, Pam.</i>

9
00:00:17,518 --> 00:00:19,162
Michael, do you need me to call an ambulance?

10
00:00:19,186 --> 00:00:20,354
<i>No! I want you to pick me up.</i>

11
00:00:20,437 --> 00:00:21,563
Okay. What's going on?

12
00:00:21,647 --> 00:00:23,374
Wait a sec. I thought you said that you were hurt.

13
00:00:23,398 --> 00:00:25,776
<i>I am hurt. I hurt my foot.</i> I'm sorry. Pam, what is going on?

14
00:00:25,859 --> 00:00:29,613
<i>I want to come to work, but I need you to come and pick me up.</i>

15
00:00:29,696 --> 00:00:32,574
<i>Oh, God!</i> Hey, whoa, Michael.

16
00:00:32,658 --> 00:00:34,993
<i>Oh, God!</i> It's... Okay. It's Jim.

17
00:00:35,077 --> 00:00:37,412
Just say again really loudly what happened.

18
00:00:37,496 --> 00:00:42,167
<i>Okay, I burned my foot very badly on my Foreman grill</i>

19
00:00:42,251 --> 00:00:45,087
<i>and I now need someone to come and bring me in to work.</i>

20
00:00:45,170 --> 00:00:48,715
You burned your foot on a Foreman grill?

21
00:00:48,799 --> 00:00:50,551
I enjoy having breakfast in bed.

22
00:00:50,634 --> 00:00:53,136
I like waking up to the smell of bacon. Sue me.

23
00:00:53,220 --> 00:00:56,139
And since I don't have a butler, I have to do it myself.

24
00:00:56,223 --> 00:00:58,809
So, most nights before I go to bed,

25
00:00:58,892 --> 00:01:02,604
I will lay six strips of bacon out on my George Foreman grill.

26
00:01:03,021 --> 00:01:06,858
Then go to sleep. When I wake up, I plug in the grill.

27
00:01:07,025 --> 00:01:08,610
I go back to sleep again.

28
00:01:08,694 --> 00:01:12,406
Then I wake up to the smell of crackling bacon.

29
00:01:13,031 --> 00:01:14,950
It is delicious. It's good for me.

30
00:01:15,033 --> 00:01:16,827
It's a perfect way to start the day.

31
00:01:17,244 --> 00:01:21,456
Today, I got up, I stepped onto the grill, and it clamped down on my foot.

32
00:01:21,540 --> 00:01:24,793
That's it. I don't see what's so hard to believe about that.

33
00:01:24,876 --> 00:01:26,461
<i>Pam, could you come get me?</i>

34
00:01:26,545 --> 00:01:29,214
I have to stay here and answer the phone.

35
00:01:29,298 --> 00:01:31,717
<i>Okay, could someone come and get me, please? Ryan?</i>

36
00:01:31,800 --> 00:01:34,678
<i>Michael, you should</i> stay home and rest. There's no toilet paper here.

37
00:01:34,761 --> 00:01:36,847
<i>Could Ryan... Tell Ryan to bring toilet paper.</i>

38
00:01:36,930 --> 00:01:38,265
<i>Could you tell him that?</i>

39
00:01:38,348 --> 00:01:40,892
<i>Can you hop?</i> I tried hopping, Kevin,

40
00:01:40,976 --> 00:01:43,520
<i>and I bumped my elbow against the wall,</i>

41
00:01:43,604 --> 00:01:46,898
<i>and now my elbow has a protuberance.</i>

42
00:01:48,817 --> 00:01:50,611
<i>No one wants to pick me up?</i>

43
00:01:52,279 --> 00:01:53,697
What is going on?

44
00:01:54,364 --> 00:01:55,699
What is going on?

45
00:01:55,907 --> 00:01:58,869
Michael is sick and he wants one of us to rescue him.

46
00:01:58,952 --> 00:02:00,552
<i>I'm not sick! I'm...</i> I'm coming, Michael!

47
00:02:00,579 --> 00:02:01,705
I'm gonna save you!

48
00:02:01,788 --> 00:02:03,624
<i>Don't! Is that Dwight? I do not want Dwight.</i>

49
00:02:03,707 --> 00:02:06,460
Okay! Hold on, Michael, I am coming! Wait there!

50
00:02:06,543 --> 00:02:08,045
<i>I don't want Dwight!</i>

51
00:02:08,128 --> 00:02:10,088
Michael, why don't you call your girlfriend?

52
00:02:10,172 --> 00:02:11,548
<i>I don't have a girlfriend.</i>

53
00:02:11,632 --> 00:02:13,443
But you said you went out with her this weekend.

54
00:02:13,467 --> 00:02:15,552
<i>That was all made up. Just someone come, okay?</i>

55
00:02:15,636 --> 00:02:17,512
<i>Anyone. Anyone, but Dwight.</i>

56
00:02:19,014 --> 00:02:20,932
What was that? What was that?

57
00:02:25,395 --> 00:02:26,813
He hit the pole.

58
00:02:28,774 --> 00:02:30,817
It's broken, right? He can't... Oh, my gosh.

59
00:02:30,901 --> 00:02:33,195
Oh, Dwight. Dwight.

60
00:02:35,113 --> 00:02:37,699
Oh, my God. Oh, my gosh. Is he okay?

61
00:02:38,617 --> 00:02:40,077
He's still driving.

62
00:02:40,911 --> 00:02:43,747
Dwight, you forgot your bumper.

63
00:02:44,623 --> 00:02:47,417
<i>Hello? Please don't send Dwight.</i>

64
00:03:24,621 --> 00:03:26,456
Morning, everyone.

65
00:03:26,540 --> 00:03:29,960
Don't freak out. I forbid anybody to freak out.

66
00:03:30,210 --> 00:03:34,172
Clearly, I have had a very serious accident, but I will recover.

67
00:03:34,297 --> 00:03:35,757
God willing.

68
00:03:35,841 --> 00:03:37,759
I just want to be treated normally today.

69
00:03:37,843 --> 00:03:40,971
Normal would actually be good, considering the trauma that I've been through.

70
00:03:41,054 --> 00:03:43,849
You missed two big conference calls today, one with corporate.

71
00:03:43,932 --> 00:03:46,101
Oh, did you explain why?

72
00:03:46,643 --> 00:03:48,979
No, I didn't mention that you cooked your foot.

73
00:03:49,062 --> 00:03:50,689
Burned my foot, Pam.

74
00:03:52,065 --> 00:03:54,860
Please stop popping my cast.

75
00:03:54,943 --> 00:03:56,153
Thank you.

76
00:03:57,654 --> 00:03:59,054
So where are you shipping your foot?

77
00:03:59,322 --> 00:04:02,117
So, where are you shipping...

78
00:04:03,827 --> 00:04:05,162
Your foot.

79
00:04:06,913 --> 00:04:08,248
Thank you.

80
00:04:09,249 --> 00:04:10,917
Pam, messages, please.

81
00:04:11,209 --> 00:04:12,461
You didn't have any.

82
00:04:12,794 --> 00:04:17,257
Really? Well, it seemed very important to you earlier

83
00:04:17,591 --> 00:04:19,968
that you needed to stay and... Do my job?

84
00:04:20,093 --> 00:04:22,971
No. Your job is being my friend, Pam.

85
00:04:23,388 --> 00:04:24,389
Ow!

86
00:04:24,473 --> 00:04:26,141
God! It slipped.

87
00:04:26,224 --> 00:04:27,434
What... Sorry.

88
00:04:27,517 --> 00:04:30,278
It's just that before, you said you didn't want any special treatment.

89
00:04:30,353 --> 00:04:32,898
I don't want any special treatment, Pam.

90
00:04:32,981 --> 00:04:36,651
I just want you to treat me like you would a family member

91
00:04:36,735 --> 00:04:39,613
who's undergone some sort of serious physical trauma.

92
00:04:39,696 --> 00:04:41,048
I don't think that's too much to ask.

93
00:04:41,072 --> 00:04:43,134
Do you want some aspirin? Because you seem a little fussy.

94
00:04:43,158 --> 00:04:45,744
No, I don't want some aspirin. Yeah, I am fussy.

95
00:04:45,827 --> 00:04:47,412
Aspirin's not gonna do a damn thing.

96
00:04:47,496 --> 00:04:50,165
I'm sitting here with a bloody stump of a foot.

97
00:04:50,332 --> 00:04:53,960
Pam, I am Assistant Regional Manager and I can take care of him.

98
00:04:54,753 --> 00:04:56,546
Part of my duties are to...

99
00:05:03,804 --> 00:05:06,431
What? Part of your duties are to what? What?

100
00:05:07,641 --> 00:05:10,352
You just said that part of your duties are to... Something.

101
00:05:10,435 --> 00:05:12,646
No, I didn't. Yes, you did. What is wrong with you?

102
00:05:12,729 --> 00:05:14,648
What is wrong with you?

103
00:05:28,495 --> 00:05:30,997
Where is my corn bread? Here you go.

104
00:05:31,081 --> 00:05:32,934
Thank you. Did you get all dark meat like I like?

105
00:05:32,958 --> 00:05:36,670
Yes, I ordered three full rotisserie chickens worth of all dark meat.

106
00:05:36,753 --> 00:05:38,421
Where are the yams? They were out of yams.

107
00:05:38,505 --> 00:05:40,340
I got you creamed spinach.

108
00:05:40,423 --> 00:05:42,551
Did you go to the one in Stroudsburg? Yes.

109
00:05:42,634 --> 00:05:44,111
And they had no yams? They had no yams.

110
00:05:44,135 --> 00:05:46,596
How strange. Because they always have yams.

111
00:05:48,390 --> 00:05:50,892
Oh, man, is that a Prism DuroSport?

112
00:05:52,060 --> 00:05:54,062
You've seen one of these? Yeah.

113
00:05:54,229 --> 00:05:55,939
They're like an iPod, only they're better,

114
00:05:56,022 --> 00:05:58,275
because they're chunkier and more solid.

115
00:05:58,358 --> 00:05:59,860
Roy gave it to me for Christmas.

116
00:05:59,943 --> 00:06:02,070
I'm trying to figure out how to put songs on it.

117
00:06:02,153 --> 00:06:03,947
Oh, no, no. Don't go there.

118
00:06:04,573 --> 00:06:08,827
I know this Russian website where you can download songs for two cents apiece.

119
00:06:08,994 --> 00:06:11,913
Really? Yeah, I'll write down the address for you.

120
00:06:12,205 --> 00:06:16,793
Only, the only thing is, is that all the songs are in Russian.

121
00:06:19,629 --> 00:06:20,881
Kidding.

122
00:06:21,673 --> 00:06:22,716
Oh.

123
00:06:24,301 --> 00:06:25,927
Why would they all be...

124
00:06:28,847 --> 00:06:30,849
Okay, see you later, Pan.

125
00:06:35,645 --> 00:06:36,730
Pan?

126
00:06:38,356 --> 00:06:40,150
Pam. Pam?

127
00:06:42,193 --> 00:06:43,486
Oh, God.

128
00:06:46,239 --> 00:06:48,575
<i>What?</i> Come here, please.

129
00:06:48,658 --> 00:06:50,410
Tell me before I come there.

130
00:06:51,494 --> 00:06:53,914
<i>I want you to rub butter on my foot.</i> No.

131
00:06:53,997 --> 00:06:57,083
<i>Pam, please? I have Country Crock.</i> No.

132
00:07:03,048 --> 00:07:06,259
Ryan! Ryan!

133
00:07:07,135 --> 00:07:08,345
Ryan!

134
00:07:08,887 --> 00:07:12,349
These covers are totally indestructible.

135
00:07:12,432 --> 00:07:13,600
Really? Yeah.

136
00:07:13,683 --> 00:07:15,852
Throw it. I promise it won't break.

137
00:07:16,019 --> 00:07:17,062
Chuck it.

138
00:07:22,442 --> 00:07:24,361
Oh, no. It's broken. What?

139
00:07:24,903 --> 00:07:27,739
No, it's fine. I told you it wouldn't break.

140
00:07:27,822 --> 00:07:30,659
You could throw it all day long. That is so cool.

141
00:07:31,368 --> 00:07:33,411
Thanks, Dwight. You're welcome.

142
00:07:36,164 --> 00:07:38,708
So, I guess Pam and Dwight are friends now.

143
00:07:39,709 --> 00:07:41,920
Oh, God, no. Dwight isn't my friend.

144
00:07:44,130 --> 00:07:46,466
Oh, my God. Dwight's kind of my friend.

145
00:07:47,467 --> 00:07:50,720
No, no. No one is helping me out at all, Mom.

146
00:07:52,722 --> 00:07:54,641
No, I'm not gonna call Jan.

147
00:07:54,724 --> 00:07:57,811
She'd just worry, drive down here and make a big thing.

148
00:08:00,313 --> 00:08:01,773
Who told you that?

149
00:08:02,565 --> 00:08:04,109
No, it was mutual.

150
00:08:05,819 --> 00:08:07,487
What is Pam doing chatting with you?

151
00:08:15,036 --> 00:08:16,538
You like candy?

152
00:08:17,372 --> 00:08:18,665
It's all right.

153
00:08:20,166 --> 00:08:23,420
'Cause you're sweeter than candy. What is wrong with you?

154
00:08:54,868 --> 00:08:57,078
Wow, you just dive right in.

155
00:08:57,328 --> 00:09:00,165
You know, around age 12, I just started going for it, you know.

156
00:09:00,248 --> 00:09:01,708
Help!

157
00:09:03,251 --> 00:09:05,128
Oh, God! Oh, help!

158
00:09:05,920 --> 00:09:07,130
Help me.

159
00:09:07,213 --> 00:09:09,758
What happened? I fell off the toilet.

160
00:09:11,468 --> 00:09:14,012
I'm caught between the toilet and the wall.

161
00:09:15,180 --> 00:09:17,265
What do you need? Not you.

162
00:09:17,724 --> 00:09:19,017
Someone else. Get Pam.

163
00:09:19,100 --> 00:09:21,436
I don't think Pam's gonna wanna come in to the men's room.

164
00:09:21,519 --> 00:09:26,399
Get Ryan. He needs to lift me, and he needs to clean me up a little bit.

165
00:09:26,483 --> 00:09:28,151
Bring a wet towel.

166
00:09:28,651 --> 00:09:31,738
Ryan is dead.

167
00:09:31,821 --> 00:09:32,864
No, he's not. Dead.

168
00:09:32,947 --> 00:09:34,866
I just saw him. No.

169
00:09:35,408 --> 00:09:39,537
Can you just get up yourself? You only grilled your foot.

170
00:09:39,621 --> 00:09:42,707
Forget it. I'll just get up myself.

171
00:09:44,375 --> 00:09:45,668
Help!

172
00:09:48,296 --> 00:09:49,631
Oh, God!

173
00:09:52,383 --> 00:09:54,803
Do you think Dwight's being a little weird today?

174
00:09:54,886 --> 00:09:57,931
No. He's actually been really nice and helpful.

175
00:09:58,681 --> 00:10:00,183
And that isn't weird?

176
00:10:02,102 --> 00:10:03,311
Well...

177
00:10:04,646 --> 00:10:06,940
Can I have everyone's attention, please?

178
00:10:07,273 --> 00:10:11,528
Phyllis. Oscar. Ryan, who is supposed to be dead.

179
00:10:12,654 --> 00:10:14,614
Can I ask you all a question?

180
00:10:14,781 --> 00:10:18,326
Do you know what it's like to be disabled? Oscar?

181
00:10:18,827 --> 00:10:20,745
I had scoliosis as a girl.

182
00:10:20,829 --> 00:10:24,582
Never heard of it. No, a real disability, not a woman's trouble.

183
00:10:24,833 --> 00:10:27,418
When I was a teenager, I was in an iron lung.

184
00:10:27,752 --> 00:10:30,547
How old are you? No, it...

185
00:10:30,839 --> 00:10:33,007
Look, the point is,

186
00:10:33,508 --> 00:10:38,138
I am the only one here who has a legitimate disability.

187
00:10:38,680 --> 00:10:42,517
Although I'm sure Stanley has had his fair share of obstacles.

188
00:10:43,351 --> 00:10:46,646
I'm not disabled, and neither are you. Okay.

189
00:10:46,938 --> 00:10:49,566
What does this look like to you, Stanley?

190
00:10:50,650 --> 00:10:52,235
Mail Boxes Etc.

191
00:10:52,318 --> 00:10:54,988
Shut it. Okay.

192
00:10:55,864 --> 00:10:57,949
Well. Well, you know what?

193
00:10:58,366 --> 00:11:02,370
Disabilities are not things to be laughed at

194
00:11:02,537 --> 00:11:05,748
or laughed about. You people are jerks.

195
00:11:06,166 --> 00:11:08,877
Imagine if you had left Stevie Wonder

196
00:11:08,960 --> 00:11:10,920
on the floor of that bathroom instead of me.

197
00:11:11,296 --> 00:11:13,381
Oh, we wouldn't. We love Stevie Wonder.

198
00:11:17,010 --> 00:11:18,636
I burned my foot!

199
00:11:19,929 --> 00:11:23,892
Okay, 20 minutes, conference room, everybody's in there!

200
00:11:25,852 --> 00:11:26,978
Dad?

201
00:11:31,816 --> 00:11:34,819
While we are waiting for our special guest to arrive,

202
00:11:35,236 --> 00:11:36,946
I wanted you all to take a look

203
00:11:37,030 --> 00:11:40,325
at a few of the many, many disabled icons

204
00:11:40,408 --> 00:11:42,952
who have contributed so much to our society.

205
00:11:43,077 --> 00:11:44,204
Quick question. Yeah.

206
00:11:44,287 --> 00:11:46,915
Why is Tom Hanks on the wall? Twice.

207
00:11:47,498 --> 00:11:51,085
Good question. <i>Forrest Gump,</i> mentally challenged.

208
00:11:51,586 --> 00:11:53,546
<i>Philadelphia,</i> AIDS.

209
00:11:53,630 --> 00:11:55,340
I think that's from <i>Big.</i>

210
00:11:56,090 --> 00:11:58,051
I don't think so. No.

211
00:11:58,218 --> 00:12:00,637
Yeah, he's dancing on a piano with Robert Loggia.

212
00:12:00,720 --> 00:12:04,474
He grew into a man overnight, rare disability. Still works.

213
00:12:06,935 --> 00:12:10,730
A crossword puzzle, Stanley? Seriously, are you learning nothing here?

214
00:12:10,813 --> 00:12:11,898
Mmm-hmm.

215
00:12:11,981 --> 00:12:13,650
What do you mean, "Mmm-hmm"?

216
00:12:13,733 --> 00:12:15,735
I mean I'm learning nothing. Okay.

217
00:12:15,818 --> 00:12:17,463
Michael Scott. I'm looking for Michael Scott.

218
00:12:17,487 --> 00:12:20,240
Yes. Right in here. Good.

219
00:12:20,406 --> 00:12:21,866
Come on in. Great.

220
00:12:22,075 --> 00:12:25,286
This, ladies and gentlemen, is our special guest.

221
00:12:26,287 --> 00:12:29,582
Sorry I'm late. Somebody parked in the handicapped parking space.

222
00:12:31,584 --> 00:12:33,670
Hey, everyone, I'm Billy Merchant.

223
00:12:33,753 --> 00:12:35,630
You may have seen me around here before.

224
00:12:35,713 --> 00:12:38,341
I'm the Properties Manager of this office park.

225
00:12:38,424 --> 00:12:39,801
You are so brave.

226
00:12:40,176 --> 00:12:41,636
You are so brave. Thank you.

227
00:12:41,719 --> 00:12:44,180
Actually, I've been meaning to come by here for a long time...

228
00:12:44,264 --> 00:12:47,475
But it's hard for you, right? Because you're in a wheelchair.

229
00:12:47,558 --> 00:12:49,602
No, I just have a lot of properties to manage.

230
00:12:49,686 --> 00:12:51,271
Let me ask you something.

231
00:12:51,354 --> 00:12:54,524
How long does it take for you to do something simple every day?

232
00:12:54,607 --> 00:12:56,651
Like brush your teeth in the morning.

233
00:12:56,734 --> 00:12:59,404
I don't know, like 30 seconds. Oh, my God.

234
00:12:59,821 --> 00:13:02,365
That's three times as long as it takes me.

235
00:13:03,241 --> 00:13:06,494
How did you get in your wheelchair? This morning?

236
00:13:06,786 --> 00:13:08,746
Just like every other morning, just climbed on in.

237
00:13:09,956 --> 00:13:12,959
Hey, hey, hey, hey! Not funny. Not funny. Hey, hey, relax.

238
00:13:13,042 --> 00:13:15,962
Just joking around here. Well, that's good.

239
00:13:16,170 --> 00:13:17,630
He still has a sense of humor.

240
00:13:17,714 --> 00:13:21,009
Listen, I've actually used a chair since I was four years old.

241
00:13:21,092 --> 00:13:24,304
I don't really notice it anymore. Well, they do. They notice it, don't you?

242
00:13:24,387 --> 00:13:28,141
You notice it. It's the first thing you saw when he rolled in here, isn't it?

243
00:13:28,558 --> 00:13:31,602
I wanna clamp Michael's face in a George Foreman grill.

244
00:13:31,686 --> 00:13:34,366
So, there were just a couple things I wanted to remind everybody of.

245
00:13:34,397 --> 00:13:36,274
Okay. First is parking.

246
00:13:36,357 --> 00:13:38,568
You can't block the freight entrance with your car

247
00:13:38,651 --> 00:13:40,028
even if your blinkers are on.

248
00:13:40,111 --> 00:13:42,155
Does anybody have any questions?

249
00:13:42,655 --> 00:13:43,823
Yes.

250
00:13:44,782 --> 00:13:45,908
Yeah.

251
00:13:47,160 --> 00:13:48,202
Yes.

252
00:13:49,370 --> 00:13:51,289
Dwight, you have your hand up.

253
00:13:54,208 --> 00:13:58,755
Ignore him. You know what? We're not that different, you and I.

254
00:13:59,255 --> 00:14:02,633
When I clamped my foot into a non-stick grill...

255
00:14:02,717 --> 00:14:04,385
You know what, Michael? Yeah.

256
00:14:04,469 --> 00:14:06,220
Let me stop you right there. Okay.

257
00:14:06,304 --> 00:14:07,430
And leave.

258
00:14:07,513 --> 00:14:09,849
Did you see <i>Born on the Fourth of July?</i>

259
00:14:10,183 --> 00:14:13,353
I was under the impression that Billy would be more like that guy.

260
00:14:13,686 --> 00:14:15,772
What's wrong with that guy? You mean today?

261
00:14:15,855 --> 00:14:18,524
He stepped on a George Foreman grill and he burned his foot.

262
00:14:18,608 --> 00:14:21,986
No, not Michael. The moon-faced kid who crashed into the pole.

263
00:14:25,114 --> 00:14:27,158
He looks like he has a concussion.

264
00:14:31,245 --> 00:14:32,288
Hey.

265
00:14:32,455 --> 00:14:36,084
I found the pudding cups you wanted at a gas station in Carbondale!

266
00:14:36,167 --> 00:14:40,380
You did it. Look at you. And with the plate and the napkin.

267
00:14:40,463 --> 00:14:42,965
Very nice. Thank you, Ryan. You are very welcome.

268
00:14:43,049 --> 00:14:44,258
Did you get the yams?

269
00:14:44,342 --> 00:14:47,553
No, the gas station in Carbondale did not have fresh yams.

270
00:14:49,555 --> 00:14:51,641
Oh, okay. I'll just have the pudding. You sure?

271
00:14:51,724 --> 00:14:53,059
Yeah. Okay.

272
00:14:53,142 --> 00:14:55,019
You know what? I feel better.

273
00:14:55,728 --> 00:14:56,997
Ryan brought me some chocolate pudding

274
00:14:57,021 --> 00:14:59,357
and his kindness healed my foot.

275
00:15:01,275 --> 00:15:04,529
Yeah, baby! I am feeling better.

276
00:15:04,821 --> 00:15:06,948
My body's literally healing itself.

277
00:15:07,365 --> 00:15:09,283
It is amazing what the human body is capable of

278
00:15:09,367 --> 00:15:11,119
when you have a powerful brain.

279
00:15:11,202 --> 00:15:13,871
<i>I ground up four extra-strength aspirin</i>

280
00:15:13,955 --> 00:15:15,665
<i>and put them in Michael's pudding.</i>

281
00:15:16,124 --> 00:15:19,919
I do the same thing with my dog to get him to take his heartworm medicine.

282
00:15:20,711 --> 00:15:24,507
Oh, finally feel the blood coursing through my foot veins.

283
00:15:27,552 --> 00:15:29,321
Okay, I think we need to take him to the hospital...

284
00:15:29,345 --> 00:15:30,346
No, no, no.

285
00:15:30,430 --> 00:15:32,432
'Cause I'm pretty sure he has a concussion.

286
00:15:32,515 --> 00:15:34,725
Oh, now you feel some compassion for him.

287
00:15:34,809 --> 00:15:37,121
He needs to go right now, and you're his emergency contact.

288
00:15:37,145 --> 00:15:39,426
I think you should go with him. Why don't you go with him?

289
00:15:39,480 --> 00:15:41,983
I barely know him. I want Michael to take me.

290
00:15:42,066 --> 00:15:44,986
I can't take you. I don't have my car, and yours is all vomitty.

291
00:15:45,069 --> 00:15:46,362
You can take my van.

292
00:15:46,446 --> 00:15:50,283
Oh, okay. That's great. No, I can't drive. Jim, why don't you drive?

293
00:15:50,658 --> 00:15:53,369
Fine. We'll go. I'm still recovering, so let's just...

294
00:15:53,453 --> 00:15:55,264
Ryan, can you get my coat, please? Slowly, slowly.

295
00:15:55,288 --> 00:15:57,039
Okay, let's just get to the elevator.

296
00:15:57,123 --> 00:15:58,666
What are you doing?

297
00:15:58,749 --> 00:16:01,002
Vietnam sounds. Stop it. Stop, stop, stop, stop.

298
00:16:02,253 --> 00:16:03,921
Tired. Dwight, you can't lay down.

299
00:16:04,005 --> 00:16:05,131
Let's take a break. Wake up.

300
00:16:05,214 --> 00:16:07,758
Wait, here, let me help you, Dwight. Come on.

301
00:16:07,842 --> 00:16:09,218
Okay, Pam. Thanks. Get up. Get up.

302
00:16:09,302 --> 00:16:11,220
- You're the best. - Just keep him awake.

303
00:16:11,304 --> 00:16:13,222
It smells like chicken soup. I know.

304
00:16:13,306 --> 00:16:15,516
I have to go to the hospital. I know.

305
00:16:15,600 --> 00:16:17,852
Where are we going? I just wanna say goodbye, okay?

306
00:16:17,935 --> 00:16:19,187
Well, I'll be back, I mean...

307
00:16:19,270 --> 00:16:21,898
Yes, I know, but it's gonna be different. Why?

308
00:16:22,231 --> 00:16:23,774
It's just hard to explain.

309
00:16:23,858 --> 00:16:27,236
Oh, Pam, you're adorable. Oh, my goodness.

310
00:16:28,404 --> 00:16:30,948
Come here. Huggy-hugs.

311
00:16:32,033 --> 00:16:33,242
Shotgun!

312
00:16:33,326 --> 00:16:35,953
You don't think you should sit in the back with Dwight?

313
00:16:36,871 --> 00:16:39,207
The rules of shotgun are very simple and very clear.

314
00:16:39,290 --> 00:16:43,211
The first person to shout "shotgun" when you're within the sight of the car

315
00:16:43,294 --> 00:16:46,130
gets the front seat. That's how the game is played.

316
00:16:46,756 --> 00:16:48,925
There are no exceptions for someone with a concussion.

317
00:16:49,258 --> 00:16:53,429
Oh, God, a minivan. What is Meredith's problem?

318
00:16:54,096 --> 00:16:57,308
Well, I think she has a kid. Yeah, she has one kid and no husband.

319
00:16:57,391 --> 00:16:59,435
She's not gonna find one driving this thing around.

320
00:16:59,519 --> 00:17:02,438
Where are we going? Come on, get inside.

321
00:17:02,522 --> 00:17:04,982
Where are we going? We're going to Chuck E. Cheese.

322
00:17:05,066 --> 00:17:08,486
Chuck E. Cheese? Oh, God, I'm so sick of Chuck E. Cheese.

323
00:17:08,569 --> 00:17:10,029
We're going to the hospital, Michael.

324
00:17:10,238 --> 00:17:12,156
I know. I'm just saying.

325
00:17:14,200 --> 00:17:16,786
Dwight, what are you drinking? I found it under the seat.

326
00:17:16,869 --> 00:17:19,038
Oh, my God. Dwight, put that down. I'm thirsty.

327
00:17:19,121 --> 00:17:20,581
No! Give the bottle to Michael.

328
00:17:20,665 --> 00:17:21,874
No! Give the bottle to Michael.

329
00:17:21,958 --> 00:17:24,293
Give it to me, Dwight. Just keep your eyes on the road.

330
00:17:24,377 --> 00:17:26,796
Give me the bottle or you're fired! You can't fire me.

331
00:17:26,879 --> 00:17:28,798
I don't work in this van. Give it to me, Dwight.

332
00:17:28,881 --> 00:17:30,258
No. Give me the bottle!

333
00:17:30,341 --> 00:17:31,944
Will you stop? Give me the bottle, Dwight!

334
00:17:31,968 --> 00:17:33,302
Michael, stop! Just give it.

335
00:17:33,386 --> 00:17:34,887
Michael, stop! Stop. Stop it!

336
00:17:34,971 --> 00:17:36,681
Stop spraying me! Give me the bottle!

337
00:17:36,764 --> 00:17:38,724
My eyes! Stop spraying me!

338
00:17:38,808 --> 00:17:40,059
Give me the bottle!

339
00:17:40,226 --> 00:17:43,312
Dwight, what is your middle name? Danger.

340
00:17:44,730 --> 00:17:46,816
Something with a "K." It's Kurt.

341
00:17:47,400 --> 00:17:49,610
Wow, I'm so sad that I know that.

342
00:17:49,694 --> 00:17:52,488
What do I write under "reason for visit"?

343
00:17:52,572 --> 00:17:53,698
Concussion.

344
00:17:56,951 --> 00:17:59,120
What did you write? Nothing.

345
00:18:00,830 --> 00:18:03,082
I wrote, "Bringing someone to the hospital."

346
00:18:03,165 --> 00:18:05,725
So you thought they meant your reason for coming to the hospital?

347
00:18:05,793 --> 00:18:08,921
No, no. You know what, Jim? This isn't about me anymore.

348
00:18:09,338 --> 00:18:12,717
I made a miraculous recovery, which is more than I can say for him.

349
00:18:12,800 --> 00:18:14,135
Come on, Dwight.

350
00:18:16,137 --> 00:18:17,847
Hi, Michael. Hi, Dwight.

351
00:18:21,934 --> 00:18:25,813
Doctor, what is more serious, a head injury or a foot injury?

352
00:18:25,896 --> 00:18:28,316
A head injury. Well, you don't have all the information.

353
00:18:28,399 --> 00:18:32,737
The foot has been fairly severely burned, and healed quickly, very quickly.

354
00:18:33,237 --> 00:18:36,949
Actually, like, suspiciously quickly. So I'm ordering a CAT scan.

355
00:18:37,533 --> 00:18:38,743
What is that?

356
00:18:38,826 --> 00:18:41,245
Look, since you have the machine up and running,

357
00:18:41,329 --> 00:18:43,581
can I just stick my foot in? We can take a look.

358
00:18:43,664 --> 00:18:47,209
Well, for a burn, you really just need to look at the outside of the foot.

359
00:18:47,293 --> 00:18:49,045
Okay, what kind of machine is that?

360
00:18:49,211 --> 00:18:51,297
Does the skin look red and swollen?

361
00:18:51,505 --> 00:18:55,051
That's what she said. That's my joke. Damn it, Dwight.

362
00:18:57,261 --> 00:19:00,640
Okay, no electronics past this point. Camera, sound equipment...

363
00:19:00,723 --> 00:19:03,768
It's okay, they're with me. No metal of any kind.

364
00:19:03,851 --> 00:19:06,604
All right, well, I guess this is where we leave you off.

365
00:19:06,687 --> 00:19:07,772
I don't wanna do this.

366
00:19:07,855 --> 00:19:10,208
You should have thought of that before you crashed your head

367
00:19:10,232 --> 00:19:14,695
on your way to pick me up. So, we'll see you when you get out.

368
00:19:15,863 --> 00:19:17,031
Oh.

369
00:19:20,451 --> 00:19:21,994
Fine. Fine.

370
00:19:36,550 --> 00:19:39,637
Dunder Mifflin, this is Pam. Dunder Mifflin, this is Jim.

371
00:19:39,720 --> 00:19:42,390
Oh, my God. What's going on? Is Dwight okay?

372
00:19:42,473 --> 00:19:44,892
<i>He should be fine, but they brought him in for a CAT scan.</i>

373
00:19:44,975 --> 00:19:47,019
I can't believe he's getting a CAT scan.

374
00:19:47,103 --> 00:19:49,730
Michael went in there with him, too. It's pretty sweet.

375
00:19:49,814 --> 00:19:51,941
<i>Really? Michael went in with him?</i> Mmm-hmm.

376
00:19:52,191 --> 00:19:53,871
<i>Wow.</i> But they shouldn't be much longer now.

377
00:19:53,901 --> 00:19:56,737
<i>So we'll be back soon.</i> Okay, that's good news.

378
00:19:58,489 --> 00:19:59,532
Yeah, no, I'll let you go.

379
00:19:59,615 --> 00:20:00,616
<i>Okay.</i> Okay.

380
00:20:00,700 --> 00:20:01,909
<i>Bye.</i> Bye.

381
00:20:09,709 --> 00:20:11,752
Hey, Oscar. What's up, Pam?

382
00:20:11,836 --> 00:20:15,089
I just wanted to let you know that Dwight's gonna be okay.

383
00:20:15,172 --> 00:20:17,812
The doctor said there's a really simple treatment for a concussion.

384
00:20:17,883 --> 00:20:19,969
So he'll probably even be back at work tomorrow.

385
00:20:20,052 --> 00:20:23,013
Okay. I just thought you'd wanna know that.

386
00:20:29,103 --> 00:20:33,733
Okay, Mr. Schrute, inhale with me on three. One, two...

387
00:20:34,150 --> 00:20:36,819
Sir! Stop that. Stop.

388
00:20:37,820 --> 00:20:38,946
<i>Stop that.</i>

